            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> So, wouldn't it be better to define the `on_attach`'s in the `lsp` directory as follows?\n\nNo? That is just a different, bespoke scheme that happens to \"work\" with `vim.tbl_deep_extend()` at the cost of changing the semantics of `vim.lsp.config` everywhere. It would be less work, and more ergonomic, to instead to \"merge\" functions somehow (e.g. by chaining them).",
